/-!
# Finite right-coset representatives for $\Gamma_1(N)$

Theorem statement: `MTT.Cohomology.gammaOne_has_finset_complement`
(`ac4dee83-611f-4f92-93b0-904f8eb5d376`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-08.

Proof: submission `aa6d2876-a5e4-4611-a5ba-4f20d13f1d4a`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-08 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let $N>0$. There is a finite set $R\subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ containing exactly one
representative of every right coset of $\Gamma_1(N)$: multiplication induces a bijection

$$
\Gamma_1(N)\times R\;\longrightarrow\;\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z).
$$

This is the finite-coset interface used to express integrals over $\Gamma_1(N)\backslash\mathfrak H$
as finite sums over translates of the standard modular fundamental domain.

**Formalization Note** The uniqueness and coverage conditions are packaged by Mathlib's
`Subgroup.IsComplement`.

## Explanation of the source proof

For every positive integer $N$, the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(N)$ has finite index in
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$. Choose a right transversal $T$ containing the identity using
`exists_isComplement_right`. The finite-index instance and `IsComplement.finite_right` imply that
$T$ is finite. Converting this finite set to a `Finset` preserves its underlying set, hence gives
the required finite complement.

<!-- Generated by add_prove2me_provenance.py -->
